---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
const items = [
  { t: 'TCB 6.1, 6.2, 6.3 and 6.4 board repairs', p: '$54.00 flat rate' },
  { t: 'PUPKIT rebuilds', p: 'All versions' },
  { t: 'Hinged and articulated microswitches (46-006B, 101-012)', p: 'New switch body on your existing actuator arm, $32.00 flat rate' },
  { t: 'Broken part duplication', p: 'Our machine shop can duplicate broken or worn parts. Send us a photo of the surviving part.' },
  { t: 'PLC programming', p: "Bought a PLC for your Burle or Philips turnstile and it won't work? We can load the proper firmware." },
  { t: 'Tomsed TUT-60 and TST-75 mechanism reconfiguration', p: 'Direction, fail-lock, fail-safe, free passage, no passage. We guide you, or ship us the mechanism.' },
  { t: 'Discontinued indicators and odd parts', p: 'Like an Alvarado LED traffic flow indicator with nine dead non-standard LEDs. We sourced them and replaced all ten.' },
];
---

<Base title="Repairs and re-manufacturing" description="Board repairs, PUPKIT rebuilds, PLC programming and part duplication for legacy turnstiles.">
  <div class="wrap rep">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>Repairs</nav>
    <div class="rep__grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h1>Repair first. Replace when it's really time.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          It's easy to throw your hands up and say "let's just replace it." But whatever wore out your equipment will still
          be there after you replace it. Water, no lubrication, no service: the new one degrades too.
        </p>
        <p>
          We'd make more money selling you something new. That isn't what we're about. We spend a lot of time on free
          diagnostics that never turn into a sale, because a customer whose turnstile works comes back when they really need a
          part. And when something is rusted through and done, we'll tell you that too.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="saw">
        <img src="/media/sabotoge.jpg" alt="Cartoon of a man sawing off the tree branch he's sitting on" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>
          Our success secret: we knowingly saw off the branch we're sitting on. Fix it right so you never call us about that
          problem again. Business has grown anyway, by referral.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <h2>What we repair and re-manufacture</h2>
    <ul class="list">
      {items.map((i) => <li><strong>{i.t}</strong><span>{i.p}</span></li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>Something else? Call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

    <h2>How you can help other customers</h2>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>We're always looking for manuals, drawings and parts lists to share in the <a href="/library/">Library</a>.</li>
      <li>Have excess turnstile components? We sometimes need samples to put parts back into production. Let's talk.</li>
      <li>
        Service providers: we're often asked to refer a reliable contractor. If you'd like to be on our referral list, tell us
        the area you cover.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .rep {
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }
  .rep h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .rep__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .saw {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--yellow-pale);
    padding: 16px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .saw figcaption {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 44px;
  }
  .list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--black);
    max-width: 900px;
  }
  .list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .plain {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .rep__grid,
    .list li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
